\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 5.  Combining the bounds  \n\nThe top and bottom regions are disjoint (they occupy rows strictly above, respectively strictly below, the uncovered squares).  Consequently the total number of tiles in any admissible tiling is at least\n\\[\n(n-1)+(n-1)=2n-2 .\n\\tag{4}\n\\]\n\nTogether with the construction (1) we obtain equality:\n\\[\n\\text{minimum number of tiles}=2n-2 .\n\\]\n\nFor the given board \\(n=2025\\),\n\n\\[\n2n-2 = 2\\cdot2025-2 = 4050-2 = 4048 .\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\\[\n\\boxed{4048}\n\\]"
